  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "Clinical term -> segmental FIELD VALUE. This is nomenclature, not a lesion table: one entry per term, and every value must already exist in the closed vocabulary of config/segmental_schema.json. It is the piece a textbook supplies — how the words map onto the taxonomy.",
    "not_a_lesion_table": "Entries name a finding or a modifier, never a diagnosis-to-anatomy bundle. 'tetralogy' is deliberately absent: it is a NAME for a combination of findings, and combinations are read off the words present, not looked up.",
    "defaults": "Where a term is ambiguous the most common form is used and flagged with `default: true` so the clinician can see and override it. A default is a clinical judgement and needs review.",
    "source": "TBD — textbook citation for the nomenclature"
